invariant: INV-17
file: poly1305_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh poly1305-avx2
reason: the AVX2 Poly1305 returns without wiping r^2 to r^8 and its two
  multipliers, so its dead frame keeps them. r and a tag seen on the
  wire give the pad, and r and the pad forge any message under that key.
  Every tag is still right, so no vector sees it. bin/poly1305_equiv_test
  copies the stack below a call and looks for each power as the call
  lays it out; the script builds it for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64, because the kernel has a body there alone.

--- old
    carry_scalar(p->h, total);
    ct_wipe(&of_r, sizeof of_r);
--- new
    carry_scalar(p->h, total);
